{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Celebrating Christmas"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Family Recipes"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe personal and regional eating habits and cooking in a range of communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le18ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> are both used to talk about past actions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to love to watch my mother cook at Christmas. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She would always clear the kitchen table and cover it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">used to</span>  to say that something happened in the past but doesn't happen any more. It uses -ed to show past tense.</p>    For example: I used to skate every winter. </br> (Before, I skated every winter, but now I don't skate.) </p> When we were children, we used to skate all day long. </br> (Before, we skated all day long, but now we don't skate all day long.)</p>  We use would to talk about both past actions and past routines.</p>   <span class=\"italic\">Would</span> refers to actions, rather than situations."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Mother used to bake at Christmastime.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She would always make several kinds of cookies.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I used to measure out the ingredients.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would help her.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect vs.  The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense when the action has some relationship to now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's look at some other ways to use the Present Perfect."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Present Perfect is used when the time period has NOT finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you haven't put everything out yet, take the time to do it now.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Present Perfect is often used when giving recent news.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I have already made one house as you can see here.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The Present Perfect is used when the time is not specific.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I've decorated it with the hard icing, chocolates.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gingerbread"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cookie that contains ginger"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You made gingerbread houses! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le18ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "con