: 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le18ob11re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le18ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn6le18ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le18ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "In this blog, we are going to build and decorate a gingerbread house.</p>I used to love to watch my mother cook at Christmas. She would always clear the kitchen table and cover it with a plastic tablecloth. I would help her measure out the ingredients. I used to place each cup of flour, teaspoon of cinnamon and tablespoon of ginger carefully in the bowl."}, {"time": "21000", "image": "engenn6le18ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Yesterday we made the traditional gingerbread dough. I've got a set of pieces here to assemble. I have already made one house as you can see here. I've decorated it with the hard icing, chocolates and of course, the customary pair of candy canes. If you haven't put everything out yet, take the time to do it now."}, {"time": "42000", "image": "engenn6le18ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "A lot of people don't eat their gingerbread houses. To me, the only thing better than making a gingerbread house is eating it! On New Years Day, mother used to cover it with a cloth and smack it with a hammer. The whole family would have gingerbread and tea! Every mouthful was heaven!"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "picture", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le18ob11re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le18ob11re2aud01", "images": []}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}]}